    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0835" n="641" xml:id="pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC(PC)/8–845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 742<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Alternate
                        Delegate to the Preparatory Commission of the United Nations</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gerig</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">u. s. urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-08T19:00:00-04:00">August 8, 1945—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6684. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preco</hi> 23. For Gerig.</p>
                <p>Our Delegation at the Potsdam Conference is not informed of any discussions
                    relating to Preparatory Commission. British Embassy here seems to be equally
                    uninformed of any discussions of this kind. Have you had any confirmation of the
                    statement made in the first sentence of your 7519, July 26, 11:00 a.m.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d742-f1"/> and your <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copre</hi> 4
                    of July 31?<anchor n="2" xml:id="d742-f2"/> We are naturally interested in any
                    developments relating to the subject of officers of ExeCom and PreCo and would
                    appreciate your communicating any such information urgently.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                        <lb/> A[lger] H[iss] </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
